  "bodyHtml": "\n\n\t\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-byline\">\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-author\"><a href=\"/archive/source-168842638426899e3410/\" rel=\"author\" class=\"url fn n\"><span>Michael Rudden</span></a></span>\n\t\t\t\t<time class=\"entry-published updated\" datetime=\"2024-09-18T13:48:07-04:00\" title=\"Wednesday, September 18, 2024, 1:48 pm\">September 18, 2024</time>\n\t\t\t\t<span class=\"comments-link\"></span>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t<div class=\"entry-content\">\n\t\t\t<p>Over 150 budding artists of all ages participated in the Guild of Harwich Artists’ seventh annual ‘Make-it-Take-it’ held in the Harwich Community Center during the recent Harwich Cranberry Arts and Music Festival.  Guild artists set up painting stations allowing participants to try various art mediums. And the proud participants got to take home what they made.  This event was made possible by a generous grant from the Harwich Cultural Council.</p>\n<p>(Attached image captions)</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Make-it-Take-it artist Imogen LaMotte from North Chatham proudly displaying her artwork.</li>\n<li>Guild artist Katherine Vacca mentoring emerging watercolor artists.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><img class=\"alignnone size-medium wp-image-7072\" src=\"/media/archive/2bb18b8aa9446b05c05150c3976a592221790c05da260f8035cf9aa7720d2eea.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"146\" height=\"300\" loading=\"lazy\" /> <img class=\"alignnone size-medium wp-image-7073\" src=\"/media/archive/63b9f8fa383ccc6045d1e5507ac882061132752fb890e4b4613de817495bbcd5.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"265\" height=\"300\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n\n\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t<footer class=\"entry-footer\">\n\t\t\t<span class=\"entry-terms category\">Posted in <a href=\"/archive/source-e23b79be08a822c7b682/\" rel=\"tag\">WHAT'S NEW</a></span>\t\t\t\t\t</footer>\n\n\t\n",
